From 4d88b133cb0ee81c769b239cfa82e44ce5ef88bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:49:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ACPICA: Derive the bus number of PCI bridges from the
 parent bridge

acpi_hw_get_pci_device_info() sets the bus number of each PCI bridge on
the path from the root bridge to the secondary bus number of the parent
bridge (or the root bridge _BBN), and then overwrites it with the
bridge's own primary bus number register.

Right after a bridge is powered up from D3cold inside its _PS0, that
register reads 0 until the OS restores the configuration space. A
PCI_Config operation region set up in that window resolves to bus 0,
and the result is cached for the lifetime of the region.

On MacBookPro16,1, the _PS0 of the Thunderbolt upstream port sets up its
PCI_Config regions in exactly that window. They resolve to 00:00.0, the
vendor mailbox at offset 0x530 reads all ones and every command times
out, adding about 18 seconds to each power-up of the controller.

Drop the primary bus number read and keep the inherited bus number. For
a configured bridge the removed read returned the same value, because it
was read at the address derived from the parent, so behaviour only
changes in the window where the register is not restored yet.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
 drivers/acpi/acpica/hwpci.c | 22 +++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/acpica/hwpci.c b/drivers/acpi/acpica/hwpci.c
index 3bd5ebc..b27e3f1 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/acpica/hwpci.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/acpica/hwpci.c
@@ -13,7 +13,6 @@ ACPI_MODULE_NAME("hwpci")
 
 /* PCI configuration space values */
 #define PCI_CFG_HEADER_TYPE_REG             0x0E
-#define PCI_CFG_PRIMARY_BUS_NUMBER_REG      0x18
 #define PCI_CFG_SECONDARY_BUS_NUMBER_REG    0x19
 /* PCI header values */
 #define PCI_HEADER_TYPE_MASK                0x7F
@@ -358,17 +357,18 @@ acpi_hw_get_pci_device_info(struct acpi_pci_id *pci_id,
 		return (AE_OK);
 	}
 
-	/* Bridge: Get the Primary bus_number */
-
-	status = acpi_os_read_pci_configuration(pci_id,
-						PCI_CFG_PRIMARY_BUS_NUMBER_REG,
-						&pci_value, 8);
-	if (ACPI_FAILURE(status)) {
-		return (status);
-	}
-
+	/*
+	 * Bridge: The bus number of the bridge itself is already known, either
+	 * from the secondary bus number of the parent bridge or from the _BBN
+	 * of the root bridge. Do not replace it with the primary bus number
+	 * register of the bridge: that register reads as zero after the bridge
+	 * has been powered up (e.g. from D3cold, while its _PS0 is executing)
+	 * and before the OS has restored its configuration space. The derived
+	 * PCI ID would then refer to bus 0, and since it is cached for the
+	 * lifetime of the operation region, all later accesses would go to
+	 * the wrong device.
+	 */
 	*is_bridge = TRUE;
-	pci_id->bus = (u16)pci_value;
 
 	/* Bridge: Get the Secondary bus_number */
 
